eveal that theme is being used for styling, but the radar/swiss distinction is actually semantic: radar=analytical/surveillance, swiss=editorial/presentation. Refactor theming to expose semantic intent (showUncertainty, emphasizeData, prioritizeReadability) rather than visual tokens.\",\"reasoning\":\"The dual-theme system encodes different user mindsets, not just color preferences. Radar users want data density and uncertainty visualization; Swiss users want clarity and narrative flow. Making this semantic would enable theme to affect behavior (show/hide confidence) not just appearance.\",\"status\":\"pending\",\"user_feedback\":null,\"user_pattern\":0,\"effort\":null,\"impact\":null,\"risk\":null,\"requirement_id\":null,\"goal_id\":null,\"created_at\":\"2026-01-30T00:19:46.171Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-01-30T00:19:46.171Z\",\"implemented_at\":null}}\r","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false}}
[2026-01-30T00:19:54.083Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_01M6Tpygu766TpmH4yd5mdir","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Report Interactive Features - Insight Synth Complete ✓\n\n**Scan ID:** `05507cf2-684b-4197-bd5f-95a7b5146287`\n\n**5 Ideas Created:**\n\n1. **Unify Attention Management Into Single Abstraction** - FocusMode, SpeedReader, SpotlightText, and KeyPointsPanel are all isomorphic attention-narrowing mechanisms (spatial, temporal, textual, importance-based). Unify into composable AttentionManager primitives.\n\n2. **Content As Stream: Temporal Reading Primitives** - Generalize SpeedReader's temporal model so any content (findings, sources, entities) can be \"played\" sequentially with configurable pacing and playback controls.\n\n3. **Confidence As First-Class UI Dimension** - Elevate confidence from metadata to a pervasive visual dimension: opacity, size, blur all proportional to certainty. Make uncertainty visible everywhere.\n\n4. **Reading Session State Machine** - Create explicit state machine tracking reading mode, position, and history to enable seamless transitions between browse/focus/speed-read while preserving context.\n\n5. **Theme As Semantic Layer Not Style Layer** - The radar/swiss themes encode user *mindsets* (analytical vs. editorial), not just colors. Refactor to expose semantic intent (showUncertainty, emphasizeData) that affects behavior, not just appearance.\n\n**Key Observation:** These components share a deep structural similarity - they're all mechanisms for controlling attention and information flow. The codebase is implicitly building an \"attention management system\" without a unified abstraction to represent it."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3653,"cache_read_input_tokens":54997,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3653},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"05d3e4f1-2259-4f3e-a055-8040a34c8b02","uuid":"ddab96e4-0b0b-4cf1-be8b-46a7e4e02b60"}
